# chat_smoke.uaw — chat round-trip smoke with model-down detection.
#
# Precondition (runner): target build installed, launched, sitting on the
# chat screen.
#
# Why this scenario exists: when the API chat model (Gemini Flash Latest)
# is down the turn ends with only the "Operit" label and NO reply body (the
# old harness read that blank body as a PASS). EXPECT_REPLY makes it a hard
# FAIL. A second guard catches the ErrorDialog form (title
# R.string.request_failed = "Request Failed") for failures that do pop it.

EXPECT 15 Enter your question...
MAYBE_TAP New Chat
EXPECT Enter your question...
REPLY_BASE
TAP Enter your question...
TYPE ping
TAP Send
# The model call spends a while in flight; wait for a real reply body.
EXPECT_REPLY 120
# Guard the dialog form of the failure too (should never show on a healthy turn).
EXPECT_ABSENT 5 Request Failed
DUMP
